": \"d143ad199d8b756c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29283613595090585, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09138315135843694, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7628931, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-18-OCR-Fallback.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee62b1908a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-18-OCR-Fallback.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-18-OCR-Fallback.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1075, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:48\", \"token_count\": 548, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edfac6fc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"7d969f7c78a9200e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2814477004903415, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09779447212905931, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7099719, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edfac6fc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:23\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-24\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Redaction Preview UI Overlay Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 11:18] Diana**: Starting on the redaction preview overlay. Users need to see what's being redacted before the final export. I'm proposing a UI overlay that shows the bounding boxes of detected PII.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 11:19] Charlie**: How are we rendering that? If we're using Electron, we can put an SVG layer over the PDF preview.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 12:54] Diana**: Got a mockup — semi-transparent red blocks for high-confidence matches, yellow for low-confidence ones that need manual review.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 14:19] Charlie**: Scroll sync needs to be exact. If the overlay drifts from the text, the whole thing is useless.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 14:32] Diana**: Using the `pdf.js` coordinate system to map the bounding boxes directly onto the viewport.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 14:36] Alice**: Can users click a box to un-redact it?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 15:00] Diana**: Not in the first version — it's just a preview for now. Toggling redactions will be part of the manual review workflow.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 15:39] Diana**: I'll share the CSS for the highlighter blocks shortly.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 24 slack thread redact preview ui overlay design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 04 2026 08 04 11 18 diana start on the redact preview overlay user need to see what s be redact befor the final export i m propos a ui overlay that show the bound box of detect pii 2026 08 04 11 19 charli how are we render that if we re use electron we can put an svg layer over the pdf preview 2026 08 04 12 54 diana got a mockup semi transpar red block for high confid match yellow for low confid one that need manual review 2026 08 04 14 19 charli scroll sync need to be exact if the overlay drift from the text the whole thing is useless 2026 08 04 14 32 diana use the pdf j coordin system to map the bound box direct onto the viewport 2026 08 04 14 36 alic can user click a box to un redact it 2026 08 04 15 00 diana not in the first version it s just a preview for now toggl redact will be part of the manual review workflow 2026 08 04 15 39 diana i ll share the cs for the highlight block short\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee1007248a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-redaction-preview-overlay.md\", \"id\": \"2de3b4a7f1d047d3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2772590064079608, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11583176915422974, \"vector_similarity\": 0.65392256, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-redaction-preview-overlay.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee1007248a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-redaction-preview-overlay.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-redaction-preview-overlay.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1196, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:03\", \"token_count\": 357, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Traced paths\\n\\nA single run of the per-page OCR fallback pool creates three categories of temporary artifact:\\n\\n1. A per-page rasterized image, one file per page, in a process-local temp directory.\\n\\n2. A per-page OCR output buffer, written before confidence-threshold filtering is applied.\\n\\n3. A run-level manifest listing which pages fell back to OCR versus native text extraction.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Purpose of this trace\\n\\nThis trace was compiled as an input to the ephemeral-file-cleanup work so that whatever cleanup mechanism is built has a concrete list of paths to target. It only records where files land and when they are created.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Open item\\n\\nConfirming that these three path categories are actually removed after a run, on both the success and failure paths, is outside the scope of this trace and is not addressed here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 trace path a singl run of the per page ocr fallback pool creat three categori of temporari artifact 1a per page raster imag one file per page in a process local temp directori 2 a per page ocr output buffer written befor confid threshold filter is appli 3a run level manifest list which page fell back to ocr versus nativ text extract sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 purpos of this trace this trace wa compil a an input to the ephemer file cleanup work so that whatev cleanup mechan is built ha a concret list of path to target it onli record where file land and when they are creat sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 open item confirm that these three path categori are actual remov after a run on both the success and failur path is outsid the scope of this trace and is not address here\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eea99e988a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"id\": \"60fa0292f9004b16\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2582436105476016, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06519631506800225, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7086873, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eea99e988a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1093, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:45\", \"token_count\": 435, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Scope of the 2026-08-09 inventory\\n\\nAn audit of the dependency tree was run to catalog every third-party license in use ahead of release, flagging anything more restrictive than a permissive license.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Finding and immediate action\\n\\nThe PDF-parsing dependency's license was flagged as a concern, and the team swapped it for a different parser library as a direct result of this inventory.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Status as of 2026-08-15\\n\\nBecause this report is written retrospectively on 2026-08-21, it can note the later developments: the replacement parser adopted from the 08-09 finding was swapped in on 2026-08-11, then the task reopened on 2026-08-12 when that replacement turned out itself to be AGPL-licensed, which is not acceptable for the shipped dependency set. By 2026-08-15 the team was searching for an Apache- or MIT-licensed alternative; that search had not concluded as of this writing.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15 retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 scope of the 2026 08 09 inventori an audit of the depend tree wa run to catalog everi third parti licens in use ahead of releas flag anyth more restrict than a permiss licens sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15 retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 find and immedi action the pdf pars depend s licens wa flag a a concern and the team swap it for a differ parser librari a a direct result of this inventori sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15 retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 status a of 2026 08 15 becaus this report is written retrospect on 2026 08 21 it can note the later develop the replac parser adopt from the 08 09 find wa swap in on 2026 08 11 then the task reopen on 2026 08 12 when that replac turn out itself to be agpl licens which is not accept for the ship depend set by 2026 08 15 the team wa search for an apach or mit licens altern that search had not conclud a of this write sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee935bb08a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"id\": \"36fdb209a7d39279\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25573097097953584, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0750840728279084, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6772404, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee935bb08a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Review-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1278, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:03\", \"token_count\": 583, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Opt-Out Behaviour Designed\\n\\nThe CLI and API collect anonymous usage metrics (pages processed, OCR fallback rate) to help tune the detection engine. Setting `CIPHER_TELEMETRY=0`, or the equivalent GUI toggle, is designed to immediately stop all outbound telemetry traffic to the metrics endpoint.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Design-Time Issue Found and Patched: Pending-Queue Leak\\n\\nWhile designing the flag semantics, testing surfaced that the opt-out flag blocked network egress correctly, but the `TelemetryLogger` kept writing event payloads to a local SQLite queue regardless. That meant re-enabling telemetry later would flush the entire backlog accumulated during the opt-out period, including events the user believed were never being recorded. The logger was patched to a no-op backend when opted out, closing that gap before the flag semantics were finalized.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Verification (Retrospective)\\n\\nA network trace on 2026-08-24 confirmed zero outbound telemetry traffic once the opt-out flag is set, closing the CLI-side verification as Completed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Remaining Limitation\\n\\nThe third-party Electron crash reporter (Sentry) has not been audited for whether it independently respects the opt-out environment variable or requires its own disable hook for minidump uploads.\\n\\n*Note*: CLI-side telemetry opt-out is verified. Full privacy compliance for air-gapped/opt-out users cannot be claimed until the Sentry cras