rategi status complet assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 06 08 descript implement fail close behavior for the batch engin so a process failur never releas an unredact output file w 04 bob complet the implement on 2026 06 15 on 2026 07 16 diana s qa pas valid the fail close behavior confirm no output file is produc on failur and that temp file are secur delet ahead of the encrypt t021 and offlin mode t027 work that depend on it clickup task ciph 25 sourc id src cu ciph 25 task id ciph 25 titl batch process fail close strategi status complet assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 06 08 activ histori\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee50b5308a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"id\": \"2bd83435b25a5e1f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2680787880289274, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0733016143270391, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72255886, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee50b5308a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1283, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:04\", \"token_count\": 638, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Traced paths\\n\\nA single run of the per-page OCR fallback pool creates three categories of temporary artifact:\\n\\n1. A per-page rasterized image, one file per page, in a process-local temp directory.\\n\\n2. A per-page OCR output buffer, written before confidence-threshold filtering is applied.\\n\\n3. A run-level manifest listing which pages fell back to OCR versus native text extraction.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Purpose of this trace\\n\\nThis trace was compiled as an input to the ephemeral-file-cleanup work so that whatever cleanup mechanism is built has a concrete list of paths to target. It only records where files land and when they are created.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Open item\\n\\nConfirming that these three path categories are actually removed after a run, on both the success and failure paths, is outside the scope of this trace and is not addressed here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 trace path a singl run of the per page ocr fallback pool creat three categori of temporari artifact 1a per page raster imag one file per page in a process local temp directori 2 a per page ocr output buffer written befor confid threshold filter is appli 3a run level manifest list which page fell back to ocr versus nativ text extract sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 purpos of this trace this trace wa compil a an input to the ephemer file cleanup work so that whatev cleanup mechan is built ha a concret list of path to target it onli record where file land and when they are creat sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 open item confirm that these three path categori are actual remov after a run on both the success and failur path is outsid the scope of this trace and is not address here\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eea99e988a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"id\": \"60fa0292f9004b16\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26250717785427863, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06501251836325517, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72332805, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eea99e988a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1093, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:45\", \"token_count\": 435, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Worker Management Decision\\n\\nRetrospective note on the concurrency block confirmed 2026-08-25. For large-scale redaction jobs, the batch API moved from a synchronous blocking loop to an `asyncio`-driven queue: a single producer walks the file system and pushes document tasks, while a fixed pool of async workers pulls from the queue and orchestrates I/O against the redaction engine, built on top of the already-completed multi-threaded worker pool (T026).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Ordering & Race Risk\\n\\nBecause documents vary widely in size, workers finish out of order. When multiple workers append to the same shared results manifest concurrently, writes can interleave and corrupt the JSON structure.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Update: Confirmed I/O Race, Throughput Regression\\n\\nConcurrency testing on 2026-08-25 confirmed the race is real, not just theoretical: under concurrent load, the race condition measurably cuts batch throughput by roughly 10% compared to the expected async speedup, because workers end up retrying/serializing around the corrupted-write recovery path. This is now blocking further rollout of the async scheduler.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nT037 is **Blocked** on resolving the manifest-write race before the async scheduler can be considered production-ready; the throughput regression it causes depends directly on how the T026 worker pool's result-writing is serialized.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 worker manag decis retrospect note on the concurr block confirm 2026 08 25 for larg scale redact job the batch api move from a synchron block loop to an asyncio driven queue a singl produc walk the file system and push document task while a fix pool of async worker pull from the queue and orchestr i o against the redact engin built on top of the alreadi complet multi thread worker pool t026 sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 order race risk becaus document vari wide in size worker finish out of order when multipl worker append to the same share result manifest concurr write can interleav and corrupt the json structur sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 updat confirm i o race throughput regress concurr test on 2026 08 25 confirm the race is real not just theoret under concurr load the race condit measur cut batch throughput by rough 10 compar to the expect async speedup becaus worker end up retri serial around the corrupt write recoveri path this is now block further rollout of the async schedul sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 status t037 is block on resolv the manifest write race befor the async schedul can be consid product readi the throughput regress it caus depend direct on how the t026 worker pool s result write is serial\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee9018c48a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"id\": \"9d00b67cdd17eab8\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2496576923157516, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04875938902250232, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7184204, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee9018c48a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1694, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:06\", \"token_count\": 573, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-28\\n\\n# Slack Thread: OCR Temp File Trace\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 10:03] Charlie**: Tracing every place the OCR branch writes a temp file. We can't add cleanup hooks until we know all the sites that actually create one.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 10:06] Alice**: How many sites so far?\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 10:19] Charlie**: More than I expected. Some go through the library's default temp handling, some are paths we wrote ourselves. They're not consistent.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 11:49] Diana**: QA saw a batch fail last week and leave a pile of orphaned temp files behind — that's probably one of the ones you haven't found yet.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 11:56] Charlie**: Probably. I'm building the full inventory now so nothing gets missed once the hooks go in.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:58] Evan**: Once you've got the list, want a second pass to confirm nothing's hiding behind a library default?\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:59] Charlie**: Yeah, that'd help. I'll share the inventory once it's done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 28 slack thread ocr temp file trace channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 07 2026 08 07 1003 charli trace everi place the ocr branch write a temp file we can t add cleanup hook until we know all the site that actual creat one 2026 08 07 10 06 alic how mani site so far 2026 08 07 10 19 charli more than i expect some go through the librari s default temp handl some are path we wrote ourselv they re not consist 2026 08 07 11 49 diana qa saw a batch fail last week and leav a pile of orphan temp file behind that s probabl one of the one you haven t found yet 2026 08 07 11 56 charli probabl i m build the full inventori now so noth get miss onc the hook go in 2026 08 07 13 58 evan onc you ve got the list want a second pas to confirm noth s hide behind a librari default 2026 08 07 13 59 charli yeah that d help i ll share the inventori onc it s done\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edc3b7988a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-07-ocr-temp-file-trace.md\", \"id\": \"dea0163e4b91c385\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2494658033157516, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04875938902250232, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71778077, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-07-ocr-temp-file-trace.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\